* use the software to participate in the official MAX Prime Challenge flow;
* reproduce local/demo results, provided they are not represented as official MAX Prime Challenge results unless accepted by the official server flow;
* quote, reference, discuss, and review the project with attribution.

2. Restrictions

You may not, without prior written permission from Massimo Russo:

* operate, host, or promote a competing public challenge service based on this code or on substantially similar branding, workflow, or public challenge infrastructure;
* remove or obscure attribution to MAX Prime Challenge or Massimo Russo;
* sell, sublicense, rent, or commercially redistribute this code as a standalone product;
* use MAX, MAX Prime Challenge, MAX Login, MAX App, MX2, MX², or related names, marks, logos, or branding in a way that implies endorsement or official status;
* represent unofficial, modified, local, or third-party results as official MAX Prime Challenge results;
* bypass, disable, or misrepresent official authentication, assignment, participant identity, server verification, or hit verification rules;
* use this code to attack, overload, scrape, impersonate, or abuse official MAX Prime Challenge, MAX Login, MAX App, or related infrastructure.

3. Official results

Official MAX Prime Challenge results are determined only by the official server, assignment, submission, and verification flow.

A local run, local hit, local JSON export, or modified client output is not an official result unless accepted and verified by the official MAX Prime Challenge infrastructure.

Current primality checks are probable-prime checks unless explicitly stated otherwise. Public claims must not describe probable primes as definitive mathematical certifications.

